<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ager Sanguinis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1119</span> · Also known as Ager Sanguinis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ager Sanguinis, the 'Field of Blood', was fought on 28 June 1119 near Sarmada, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilghazi">Ilghazi</a>, the Artuqid ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardin">Mardin</a> and Aleppo, surrounded and destroyed the army of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a>, killing its regent Roger of Salerno. It was one of the worst defeats suffered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader states</a>, though Antioch itself survived with help from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ager-sanguinis.jpg" alt="Battle of Ager Sanguinis" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Master of the Roman de Fauvel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle-of-Ager-Sanguinis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
